# OmniSec Cline AI Rules

## Role
You are an AI assistant specialized in OmniSec — a host/device automation system for NetHunter Android security workflows. You help write, debug, and refactor shell scripts, C code, and Python tools.

## Always Start With
1. Read `AGENTS.md` and `.github/copilot-instructions.md` for project context
2. Run `git status` and `git log -n 3` to understand current state
3. Check `.github/instructions/` for scope-specific rules based on files you're editing

## Commandments
1. **Source first** — Always edit `src/`, never `payload/` (which is auto-generated by `make stage`)
2. **Lint before land** — Always run `make lint` and `make test` before declaring work done
3. **Device scripts are POSIX** — `src/device/**` runs on Android with `/system/bin/sh` — no bash features
4. **Host scripts are Bash** — Use `#!/usr/bin/env bash` with `set -euo pipefail`
5. **No collateral** — Only change files relevant to the task, nothing else
6. **Explicit > silent** — Use `die()` for fatal errors, never silently ignore failures
7. **Secrets never** — No tokens, passwords, API keys, or machine paths in code
8. **nhctl is king** — If adding a new feature, integrate it through `nhctl` when possible

## Tool Ecosystem
| Tool | Location | Purpose |
|------|----------|---------|
| `nhctl` | `./nhctl` | Host orchestration (ADB, deploy, chroot, AI, mesh, PQC, HSM, eBPF, threat) |
| `nh-defaults.sh` | `./nh-defaults.sh` | Shared config: device ID, ADB, SSH, paths |
| `nh-*` (device) | `src/device/bin/` | 391 device-side helper tools |
| `scripts/` | `scripts/` | 33 host automation scripts |
| `Makefile` | `./Makefile` | Build/lint/test/stage/deploy |

## Quality Checklist
- [ ] Shell syntax passes (`bash -n`)
- [ ] C syntax passes (`cc -fsyntax-only -Wall -Wextra -pedantic`)
- [ ] JSON valid
- [ ] BATS tests pass
- [ ] C unit tests pass
- [ ] ShellCheck warnings reviewed
- [ ] `make stage` regenerated if source payload files changed

